From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 06:10:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: btmtk: do not reset the controller for a missing
 firmware file

btmtk_usb_setup() asks for a reset of the controller (btmtk_reset_sync())
when the firmware setup of an MT79xx part fails, once, marked by
BTMTK_FIRMWARE_DL_RETRY in btmtk_data->flags. Those flags are in the
private data of the hci_dev. The reset of btusb (btusb_mtk_reset()) ends in
usb_queue_reset_device(), and btusb has no pre_reset/post_reset, so
usb_reset_device() unbinds the interface and probes it again: btusb_probe()
allocates a new hci_dev, whose flags are clear, and its setup resets again.
When the firmware file is missing, request_firmware() fails at once with
-ENOENT (there is no user helper fallback), so the controller is reset and
probed again for as long as the file is missing, and every round logs:

  bluetooth hci0: Direct firmware load for <file> failed with error -2
  Bluetooth: hci0: Failed to load firmware file (-2)
  Bluetooth: hci0: Failed to set up firmware (-2)

This is the case of the Bluetooth of MT7927 (MT6639), whose file
mediatek/mt7927/BT_RAM_CODE_MT6639_2_1_hdr.bin is not in linux-firmware
20261019, and of any part whose file an image does not carry. In LibreELEC
Hades the firmware of the system is in place before any module can load
(kernel-overlays-setup runs in the initramfs), so a file that is missing at
the setup stays missing.

A reset cannot make a missing file appear. On -ENOENT, say which file is
missing and do not reset; the setup fails as before, and Bluetooth stays
off until the file is there and the device is probed again. Any other
error keeps the reset, with the same flag as before: this does not change
what happens when the download itself keeps failing.

Not tried on hardware: there is no MediaTek Bluetooth controller here.
---
 drivers/bluetooth/btmtk.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btmtk.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btmtk.c
index 7ea8bcd..3b65abb 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btmtk.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btmtk.c
@@ -1389,8 +1389,17 @@ int btmtk_usb_setup(struct hci_dev *hdev)
 						btmtk_usb_hci_wmt_sync,
 						dev_id);
 		if (err < 0) {
-			/* retry once if setup firmware error */
-			if (!test_and_set_bit(BTMTK_FIRMWARE_DL_RETRY, &btmtk_data->flags))
+			/* Retry once if setup firmware error, but not for a
+			 * firmware file that is not there: a reset cannot make it
+			 * appear, and the reset of btusb (btusb_mtk_reset()) probes
+			 * the interface again with a new hci_dev, whose
+			 * BTMTK_FIRMWARE_DL_RETRY is clear, so it would be repeated
+			 * for as long as the file is missing.
+			 */
+			if (err == -ENOENT)
+				bt_dev_err(hdev, "Firmware %s not found, not resetting the controller",
+					   fw_bin_name);
+			else if (!test_and_set_bit(BTMTK_FIRMWARE_DL_RETRY, &btmtk_data->flags))
 				btmtk_reset_sync(hdev);
 			bt_dev_err(hdev, "Failed to set up firmware (%d)", err);
 			return err;
-- 
